# {{lb|en|slang}} [[balderdash|Balderdash]]!, [[nonsense]]!, [[rubbish#Interjection|rubbish]]!
#* {{quote-journal|en|title=Ambition. A Farce.|magazine=[[w:Blackwood's Magazine|Blackwood's Edinburgh Magazine]]|location=Edinburgh; London|publisher=[[w:Blackwood (publishing house)|William Blackwood & Sons]]|month=October|year=1841|volume=L|issue=CCCXII|page=438|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=iWlHAQAAMAAJ&pg=PA438|oclc=702604824|passage=[''Mr. Clarendon''] ''Steady.'' Aristotle laughs at you. / [''Mr. Algernon Sidney''] ''Twist.'' He's an impertinent fellow! I say again—Liberty! freedom! glory! / ''Steady.'' '''Humbug'''! '''humbug'''! '''humbug'''!}}
#* {{RQ:Dickens Christmas Carol|chapter=Stave I. Marley’s Ghost.|pages=6–7|pageref=7|passage="A Merry Christmas, uncle! God save you!" cried a cheerful voice. It was the voice of Scrooge’s nephew, who came upon him so quickly that this was the first intimation he had of his approach. / "Bah!" said Scrooge, "'''Humbug'''!" / {{...}} "Christmas a humbug, uncle!" said Scrooge's nephew. "You don't mean that, I am sure." / "I do," said Scrooge. "Merry Christmas! what right have you to be merry? what reason have you to be merry? You're poor enough." / "Come, then," returned the nephew gaily. "What right have you to be dismal? what reason have you to be morose? You're rich enough." / Scrooge having no better answer ready on the spur of the moment, said, "Bah!" again; and followed it up with "'''Humbug'''."}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:Guy de Maupassant|chapter=Magnetism|title=Ball-of-Tallow and Short Stories|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher=[[w:Pearson PLC|The Pearson Publishing Co.]]|year=1910|page=302|pageurl=https://archive.org/stream/balloftallowand00maupgoog#page/n312/mode/1up/|oclc=4175409|passage=Then each mentioned some fact, some fantastic presentiment, some instance of souls communicating with each other across space, or some case of the secret influence of one being over another. They asserted and maintained that these things had actually occurred, while the sceptic angrily repeated: / "'''Humbug'''! '''humbug'''! '''humbug'''!"}}

